  "worked_solution": "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-1)^{3}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-7x+8 & =A(x-1)^{2}+B(x-1)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(1)^{2}-7(1)+8 & =A(1-1)^{2}+B(1-1)+C \\\\ 4 & =A(0)+B(0)+C \\\\ C & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(0)^{2}-7(0)+8 & =A(0-1)^{2}+B(0-1)+4 \\\\ 8 & =A-B+4 \\\\ 0 & =A-B-4 \\\\ B & =A-4.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x=2$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(2)^{2}-7(2)+8 & =A(2-1)^{2}+B(2-1)+4 \\\\ 6 & =A+B+4 \\\\ 0 & =A+B-2 \\\\ B & =2-A.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-4 & =2-A \\\\ 2A & =6 \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $A$ into $(2)$  to get the value of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =3-4=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cdot B\\cdot C & =3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 4=-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
